\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Reading a loop at two times}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{In the [SU(2) heat-kernel model](fdip-00MM), a spatial
 plaquette has an ordered holonomy and a real trace. The
 [periodic trace law](fdip-0083) places a bounded function of
 that trace at a chosen time slice, with transfer factors between
 slices. Two such insertions leave two lengths of propagation
 around the time circle. As one length grows, which part of the
 physical transfer spectrum determines the limiting state and
 the dependence on the remaining separation?}
